  "body": "The v0.4.1 installer could not install on machines with python3 because a heredoc consumed the release JSON. This release fixes that.\n\n- Python reads the release JSON from stdin. Asset names are matched exactly, so a `.sig` file is not selected by substring.\n- Unknown arguments such as `--unistall` fail instead of installing.\n- v0.4.0 is refused and withdrawn.\n- Default state directory is `~/.config/paradise` (directory 0700, files 0600), not the working tree and not `/tmp`.\n- The binary no longer embeds `/home/ubuntu`, SSH operator commands, or `cargo run` instructions.\n- Linux x86_64 and macOS are still not published. The installer says so and exits.\n\nSHA-256 of `paradise-aarch64-linux` is in `SHA256SUMS`. That file is not signed. A signature key is not stored in this GitHub account yet."
